/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Yes. Although AB 126 does not require public school employers and community college districts to provide Paid Pregnancy Leave until January 1, 2027, a local union may bargain for a more generous benefit, including an earlier implementation date. California law generally permits collective bargaining over contractual provisions that provide employees with greater rights or benefits than those guaranteed by the Education Code, as long as the negotiated agreement does not conflict with or reduce the statutory protections)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 62 0 R
/T (MY LOCAL CHAPTER NEGOTIATED PAID BABY BONDING LEAVE IN OUR CONTRACT. CAN THE EMPLOYER SUPPLANT THE CONTRACTUAL BABY BONDING LEAVE WITH PPL?)
/E (MY LOCAL CHAPTER NEGOTIATED PAID BABY BONDING LEAVE IN OUR CONTRACT. CAN THE EMPLOYER SUPPLANT THE CONTRACTUAL BABY BONDING LEAVE WITH PPL?)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (Generally, no. AB 126 provides that PPL does not diminish an employer's obligation to comply with a collective bargaining agreement that provides greater disability or parental leave rights than those established by AB 126)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
